CYBER QUEST - PORTABLE EDITION (Windows)
========================================

WHAT THIS IS
A self-contained copy of Cyber Quest. It includes its own Java runtime and a
file-based database, so you do not need to install Java, Docker or PostgreSQL.

HOW TO START
1. Extract the WHOLE zip to a normal folder (Desktop, Documents or a USB drive).
   Do not run it from inside the zip, and avoid C:\Program Files.
2. Double-click  start.bat
3. First time only: type a password for the manager and the employee account.
4. Your browser opens at http://localhost:8080
   Sign in as  manager@cyberquest.internal  or  employee@cyberquest.internal

HOW TO STOP
Double-click  stop.bat  when you are finished.

WHERE YOUR DATA IS
The  data  folder holds the database. Copy the whole folder to back it up or to
move the program to another computer. Delete the  data  folder to start fresh
(this erases all users and scores).
The  logs  folder holds cyberquest.log, useful if something goes wrong.

GOOD TO KNOW
- Only this computer can reach the program (it listens on 127.0.0.1).
- Run only one copy at a time. It uses port 8080.
- Windows may say "Windows protected your PC" the first time. Choose
  "More info" and then "Run anyway". The files are not digitally signed.
- The practice phishing emails stay inside the program. Nothing is sent out.
- The mock HR import is not included in this edition.

IF IT DOES NOT START
- Read the last lines of logs\cyberquest.log.
- Make sure nothing else uses port 8080 (run stop.bat, then start.bat again).
- Make sure you extracted every file (the runtime folder must exist).
